--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- chain in a MoorDyn-C wave record (WaveKin 3) and a current varying in time (Currents 2), 120 s
-- The 410 m studless chain of dynamic_chain_waves.dat with its anchor 390 m from the held
-- fairlead in 50 m of water: about 90 m hangs free and the rest lies on the seabed, held by
-- seabed friction (0.7). The water kinematics come from MoorDyn-C's fixed-name files in this
-- folder (generate_kinematics.py writes them). WaveKin 3 reads wave_elevation.txt, `time
-- elevation` rows from t = 0 without a header: here 280 s of a bimodal swell at the origin
-- (1.0 m at 10 s and 0.6 m at 14 s, travelling along +X). CableDyn resamples it at dtWave,
-- reduces it to its Fourier components up to WvHiCOff (0.5 Hz) and evaluates them at every node
-- with Wheeler stretching. Currents 2 reads current_profile_dynamic.txt, a depth profile in
-- time: line 5 lists the depths, each later row `t ux(z1..zn) uy(z1..zn)`. Here the current,
-- sheared from 30 % of its surface speed at the seabed, turns from along the line (+X) to
-- across it (+Y) while its surface speed grows from 0.5 to 1.0 m/s; it is linear in time between
-- rows, carries no fluid acceleration, and the static start takes its t = 0 profile, as
-- MoorDyn-C does. The hanging chain swings out of its plane as the current turns across it:
-- L1N5px and L1N5py track the node 40 m from the fairlead.
